  "root_cause_scope": {
    "finding": "Pinned111 packet descriptor table has44 entries, includes133-146 but no147/1ff. Separate RX event dispatch also lacks147/1ff. Replacing test-not-exercised146 entries permits exact1ff/02 real peer delivery.",
    "runtime_path": [
      "RAM1812 handler0x41a606 packs index/length/body and queues message0xb0006; Complete is constructed separately",
      "RAM message table0x41c0a0 maps0xb0006 to ROM0x14db30",
      "ROM0x14db30 looks up packet index via0x14c124; bit0 of descriptor byte4 selects a queue when state byte285 is nonzero",
      "ROM0x14c124 calls RAM0x400be0 ->0x41790a, which returns44 rows at0x41c0d4; lookup stride6",
      "RX event rows133-146 point to common0x41a6a4; this is a separate table from packet descriptors"
    ],
    "causal_evidence": "Both packet tables plus receiver dispatch (three changed rows) deliver; same native TX-only + receiver-dispatch-only configuration fails without receiver packet descriptor. Four-row variant also delivers. Stock before/after variants fail with exact original bytes loaded.",
    "not_claimed": [
      "Each of the three changes individually necessary: not all subsets tested",
      "All firmware/ROM behavior formally proved",
      "Actual over-air packet capture or PHY sniffer",
      "Stock111 production repair",
      "All security methods, key install, encryption, Bond or natural recovery"
    ]
  },
